<p>The chart and the application carry separate versions. Keep the gateway and broker on one application release, and follow the <a href="{{ source }}/docs/upgrading.md">upgrade guide ↗</a> when you replace them.</p>
<p>The archives and the image also carry <a href="{{ source }}/crates/dekopon-console/README.md"><code>dekopon-console</code> ↗</a>, an optional operator client; Homebrew installs it separately with <code>brew install dekopon-agents/tap/dekopon-console</code>. It doesn't support OpenRouter models, and the Mac Slack path doesn't need it. The chart can run it idle for <a href="/deploy/kubernetes/#pod"><code>kubectl exec</code></a>.</p>
</section>
<section id="configure">
<h2>The broker needs a provider and an explicit grant</h2>
<p>The broker needs installed providers, identities, policy and execution constraints. Release archives carry no providers and the image carries only <code>cli-probe</code> and <code>http-probe</code>; install reviewed providers yourself, or write one with the <a href="/guides/provider-sdk/">SDK guide</a>. The gateway needs a chat transport, a model endpoint and an agent catalog. The gateway holds chat and model credentials and the broker holds provider credentials; neither receives the other's. Set up <a href="/guides/traces/">telemetry collection</a> before you grant the agent useful access: the audit record lives only in the trace.</p>
<p>The <a href="{{ site.repository }}/blob/main/examples/slack-github/README.md">Slack GitHub reviewer recipe ↗</a> has a pinned provider and a complete read-only configuration for two people in one channel.</p>
<p>Check both files before you deploy: <code>dekopon-gatewayd check gatewayd.yaml --catalog agents.d</code> and <code>dekopon-brokerd check broker.yaml</code>. A broker with a managed provider set also needs <code>--provider-set</code> and a private <code>--store</code>, and its check may fetch the pinned components; deploying that set needs <a href="/deploy/kubernetes/#providers">sync and precompile</a>. Neither check proves that the socket, credentials or external services work. <code>dekopon-gatewayd check --probe</code> sends one short, paid completion to each API-key model's vendor.</p>
</section>
